  {
    "username": "emollick",
    "nickname": "Ethan Mollick",
    "text": "This paper shows why I am skeptical of the idea that frontier models can be easily replaced by cheaper ones (and why you should use the best models as orchestrators): Small improvements in accuracy & judgement compound over long-horizon tasks, creating huge gains in outcomes.",
    "quoted_tweet": null,
    "url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2110918113550307778",
    "time": "2026-10-16 10:17",
    "created_at": "Fri Oct 16 02:17:51 +0000 2026",
    "id_str": "2110918113550307778",
    "is_retweet": false
  },
  {
    "username": "emollick",
    "nickname": "Ethan Mollick",
    "text": "You may save money in the short term, at the expense of worse work at the end. That doesn't mean small models can't do tons of valuable work, but you want to make sure they are orchestrated and error-checked by larger ones for many kinds of tasks.\n\nPaper: https://arxiv.org/pdf/2509.09677",
    "quoted_tweet": null,
    "url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2110919225459998776",
    "time": "2026-10-16 10:22",
    "created_at": "Fri Oct 16 02:22:16 +0000 2026",
    "id_str": "2110919225459998776",
    "is_retweet": false
  },
